Yes, exactly. Looking at the code in `cargo_build.rs`:

```rust
fn requires_nightly(spec: &Spec) -> bool {
    let has_build_std = spec.rustc.iter().any(|p| matches!(p, RustcParam::BuildStd(_)));
    let has_unstable = !spec.cargo.unstable.is_empty();

    has_build_std || has_unstable
}
```

If `unstable` has a value, it triggers `cargo +nightly` and passes `-Z <value>`.

So the name "unstable" is really about cargo's `-Z` flags. Maybe a clearer name would be `z_flag` or `nightly_flag`? Or even just keep it as a single `Option<String>` since in practice it's only ever one value (`panic-immediate-abort`)?

